# SMILE 7.2.0 Release Notes

Welcome to **SMILE 7.2.0**! This release unifies high-performance JVM machine learning with autonomous, always-on agentic operations. Building on the 7.x architecture, **SMILE 7.2.0** introduces the **24/7 Autonomous Agent Hub & Bot Service** (`smile hub`) with human-in-the-loop approval queues, native Email and Calendar integrations with one-click Google and Microsoft OAuth login, **MiniMax-M3 & MiniMax-M3.1-Flash** multimodal LLM serving with DSpark speculative decoding and 8-GPU / multi-node execution, **Qwen3.8-27B-FP8** single-A100 serving via Marlin block-FP8 and fused DeltaNet decode kernels, first-class **Clustering, Vector Quantization, and Anomaly Detection** model serving (`ClusteringModel`, `VectorQuantizerModel`, `AnomalyModel`) with online model updates, an interactive DataFrame table viewer and rich GFM Markdown preview in Studio, model-agnostic KernelSHAP explainability, a pure-Java BLAS/LAPACK fallback engine, and comprehensive stability hardening across Studio, Serve, and the Agent harness.

---

## ✨ New Features

### 🤖 Autonomous Agent Hub, 24/7 Bots & AI Agent Workspace
- **🕒 Always-On Agent Hub & Bot Service (`smile hub`)**:
  - Introduced `smile hub`, a background runtime service for scheduled (`cron` and interval timers) and event-driven (`email`, `calendar`, `webhook`) autonomous Bot routines across all nine specialist personas (`@frank`, `@steve`, `@julien`, `@mike`, `@clair`, `@ada`, `@james`, `@guido`, `@chuck`).
  - Integrated **Bots** explorer tab, **Bot Routines** configuration manager, and **Bot Activities** workspace tab in SMILE Agent Studio with real-time Server-Sent Events (SSE) run and transcript streaming.
  - Added **Human-in-the-Loop Batch Draft Queue** with a structured review composer and formatted JSON inspector so outbound emails and calendar actions never leave your machine without explicit approval.
  - Added live **Bot Pages** (`bot-activity.html`, `executive-brief.html`, `sales-pipeline.html`, `community-pulse.html`) that automatically open or refresh in the system browser when updated by a routine.
- **📧 Unified Email & 📅 Calendar Integrations (`Email` & `Calendar` Tools)**:
  - Built-in `Email` tool (`list_accounts`, `search`, `read`, `draft`, `send`, `reply`) supporting Gmail (Primary inbox), Microsoft 365, and custom IMAP/SMTP accounts with preserved `In-Reply-To` / `References` threading and automatic IMAP `Sent` folder sync.
  - Built-in `Calendar` tool (`list_accounts`, `list_events`, `get_event`, `free_busy`, `create_event`, `update_event`, `delete_event`, `respond_invite`) supporting Google Calendar, Microsoft Graph Calendar, and `.ics` feeds.
  - **One-Click Login with Google & Login with Microsoft** in `SettingsDialog` using loopback PKCE OAuth flows, identity discovery, and sealed credential storage in `SecretStore`.
- **🌐 Agent Registry & Discovery (`SearchAgent` & `BotConfig` Tools)**:
  - Added `SearchAgent` to discover local peers (`@name`) and remote agents (`did:aid:...`) across the Agent Registry by capability or free-text query.
  - Added `BotConfig` so agents can inspect and propose routine updates with user approval.
- **🖥️ Desktop Operator (`@chuck`) & 👔 Chief of Staff (`@frank`)**:
  - Specialized desktop automation agent (`@chuck`) for GUI interaction via screenshot analysis, mouse navigation, and keyboard control with interactive confirmation.
  - Chief of Staff agent (`@frank`) for multi-agent coordination, status synthesis, priority tracking, and cross-agent briefings.

### ⚡ High-Performance LLM & Model Serving (`smile-serve` & `smile-deep`)
- **MiniMax-M3 & MiniMax-M3.1-Flash Multimodal & Distributed Serving**:
  - Full support for **MiniMax-M3** and **MiniMax-M3.1-Flash**: Multi-head Sparse Attention (MSA), block-sparse prefill and decode attention, expert parallelism across 8 GPUs (NVFP4 / MXFP8 on Marlin and block FP8), and multi-node distributed execution (leader/follower control channel, multi-process NCCL communicator, mirrored executor calls).
  - **DSpark Speculative Decoding** for MiniMax-M3.1-Flash with batched drafting, multimodal speculation, and optional draft model loading.
  - **Multimodal Image & Video Input**: CLIP-style ViT vision encoder with 3D RoPE, projector, and 2×2 patch merger, with per-block vision activation freeing and clean HTTP 400 validation for media errors.
  - Fused decode kernels (Gemma RMSNorm, QK norm + RoPE, `swigluoai`, MoE routing), single-GEMM `q/k/v/index` projections, two-kernel MSA decode scorer, and full-step CUDA-graph capture for batch sizes up to 32.
- **Qwen3.x Block-FP8 on Ampere/Ada & Ultra-Fast Fused Decode**:
  - Added Marlin FP8 kernels for block-scaled checkpoints on Ampere/Ada GPUs, enabling **Qwen3.8-27B-FP8** (including its MTP head installed directly from FP8) to run on a single 40 GB A100 without dense projection shells.
  - Fused DeltaNet core (`conv + split + gates + recurrent` in two kernel launches) and register-resident recurrent kernel split over $V$ (reducing per-layer decode latency from $122\,\mu\text{s}$ to $10\,\mu\text{s}$), plus fused verify windows with checkpoints, fused `a/b` GEMV, strided QK norm + RoPE, and fused residual-add + Gemma RMSNorm.
  - Enabled decode CUDA graphs by default with fixed-address FlashInfer page tables refreshed before each replay, and rendered prompts with the checkpoint's native chat template (thinking, reasoning effort, tools, vision).
- **Clustering, Vector Quantization & Anomaly Detection Serving**:
  - Extended `/api/v1/smile`, `smile train`, `smile predict`, and Studio's Kernel Explorer to serve serialized **Clustering** (`ClusteringModel`), **Vector Quantization** (`VectorQuantizerModel`), and **Anomaly Detection** (`AnomalyModel`) models alongside classification and regression.
  - Added **online model updates** (`update`) across `VectorQuantizerModel` and supported incremental learners.
- **Batched Multi-Token Prediction (MTP) & Interactive SHAP Explanations**:
  - High-throughput batched MTP speculative decoding with persistent per-request draft histories.
  - Native SHAP explanation payloads (`TreeSHAP`, `LinearSHAP`, and `KernelSHAP`) in REST and streaming inference responses, with interactive **Waterfall**, **Force**, and **Decision** plots in the Web UI and per-request `?samples` and `?ridge` tuning.
- **Four Container Image Flavors & Pluggable SPIs**:
  - Tailored container images: **`Dockerfile.micro`** (`-micro`, ~205 MB GraalVM native), **`Dockerfile.native`** (`-native`, ~375 MB), **`Dockerfile`** (`latest`, ~575 MB), and **`Dockerfile.gpu`** (`-gpu`).
  - Extracted Prometheus metrics (`ModelMetricsBinder`, `LlmMetrics`) and S3 blob storage into modular plugins loaded from `serve/plugins/`, keeping core images lean.
  - Hardware execution provider support for `onnxruntime-genai-directml` on Windows, `onnxruntime-genai-cuda` on Linux, and `ep-mlx` on macOS.

### 📓 Interactive Notebooks, Editors & Polyglot Data Science
- **📊 Interactive DataFrame Table Viewer for Tabular Files**:
  - Opening tabular data files (CSV, TSV, ARFF, Parquet, Avro, SAS, Feather) in Studio now opens an interactive `DataFrame` table viewer with a 100 MB large-file warning threshold and customizable row-limit prompt.
- **📝 GitHub-Flavored Markdown Preview in Notepad**:
  - Added per-file **Edit / Preview** overlay toggle buttons in the top-right of Notepad for Markdown files, rendering GFM tables, strikethrough, autolinks, and theme-aware code blocks and table headers.
- **🚀 Native Kotlin & AST-Aware Scala 3 Kernels**:
  - Interactive Kotlin notebooks (`.kts`) via the Kotlin Custom Scripting Host API and AST-aware Scala 3 REPL evaluation (`ScalaKernel`) alongside Java 25 JShell and Python/Jupyter kernels.

### 📈 Machine Learning, Analytics & Core Engine
- **First-Class Unsupervised & Anomaly Model Wrappers (`smile-core`)**:
  - Added schema-aware `ClusteringModel`, `VectorQuantizerModel`, and `AnomalyModel` records for unified serialization (`.sml`), batch CLI training/prediction, and REST serving.
- **Model-Agnostic KernelSHAP (`smile.feature.importance.KernelSHAP`)**:
  - Brought SHAP feature attributions to all DataFrame and linear models (Logistic Regression, LDA, QDA, RDA, Fisher, MLP, SVM, RBF networks, OLS, Lasso, ElasticNet, Ridge, and Gaussian Process) alongside exact TreeSHAP.
- **Pure-Java BLAS & LAPACK Fallback (`smile.linalg`, `smile.tensor`)**:
  - Pure-Java Level-1/2/3 BLAS (`JBlas`) and LAPACK decompositions/solvers (`JLapack`: LU, Cholesky, QR, SVD, EVD, banded solvers) for `Float64` and `Float32` so `smile.tensor` works out of the box without native OpenBLAS/LAPACK installed.
- **Time Series (ARIMA & ARMA), HPO & LOF Anomaly Detection**:
  - `smile.timeseries.ARIMA` and `ARMA` with AIC/BIC/log-likelihood diagnostics and coefficient $t$-tests, unit-hypercube `smile.hpo.ParameterSpace`, `smile.anomaly.LOF<T>`, and `smile.feature.selection.EnsembleSelection`.

### 📚 Expanded Skills & Extensibility
- **Document Processing & Research Skills**:
  - Built-in skills for **Excel (`excel-processing`)**, **Word (`word-processing`)**, **PDF (`pdf-processing`)**, **Deep Research (`research`)**, **Weekly Briefing (`weekly-briefing`)**, **Daily Recap (`daily-recap`)**, **Daily Log (`daily-log`)**, **Humanize (`humanize`)**, **Grill (`grill`)**, **Changelog (`changelog`)**, **Git Commit (`git-commit`)**, and **Skill Creator (`skill-creator`)**.
